# Fixtures that render and validate in scripts/test-charts.sh but cannot converge here.
# One case name per line; scripts/e2e-test.sh skips them in the default sweep and still
# runs them when E2E_CASES names them explicitly.

# Needs an SSH forge, a deploy key and pinned host keys. Nothing in CI provides one, and a
# sidecar pointed at an unreachable remote crash-loops rather than converging.
git-sync
# Needs a reachable app-set repository with an applications.yaml in it. The controller
# would come up and retry forever, which asserts nothing the `dir` fixture does not.
git-appset
# ACME cannot be exercised in CI (no public DNS, no cert issuance). `edge` covers the
# routing contract over plain HTTP.
traefik-tls
# The rotated config name (swarmcli-cd-applications_<version>) and the two registry-auth
# secrets would all have to be provisioned to assert what the `default` fixture already
# asserts about a running controller.
prune
# Host-path persistence writes to /opt/swarmcli-cd-data on the runner. The bind render is
# covered by charts.yml; still runs in local `make e2e` when named explicitly.
bind-mount
# A TLS listener needs a real certificate and single sign-on needs a reachable identity
# provider; CI has neither, and the controller exits before its listener binds when given
# a path nothing delivers. The render contract is what matters and charts.yml asserts it.
listener-tls-sso
